    <statement><p>(6 points)</p>
<p><alert> On your solution paper,  </alert>
write the <m>x=0</m>, <m>y=0</m>, <m>z=0</m> traces of each of the equations below
and identify each trace as an ellipse, parabola, or hyperbola.</p>
<p>Then match each quadric surface with its name.</p>
<p><ol>
<li>
<p><m>\phantom{^2}z = 2 x^{2} + 2 y^{2}</m></p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>\phantom{^2}z =  y^{2} - 3 x^{2}</m></p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>z^{2} = 3 x^{2} + 3 y^{2}</m></p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>z^{2} = 2 x^{2} + 3 y^{2} - 3</m></p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>\phantom{^2}1 =  x^{2} +  y^{2} + 3 z^{2}</m></p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>z^{2} = 3 x^{2} + 2 y^{2} + 3</m></p>
</li>
</ol></p>
<p><ol label="A.">
<li>
<p>hyperbaloid of one sheet</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>hyperbolic paraboloid</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>elliptical cone</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>hyperbaloid of two sheets</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>elliptical paraboloid</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>ellipsoid</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</statement>
